<tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/128"><tei:pb n="472" ed="1949 shabbat/minchah" facs="https://archive.org/download/PhilipBirnbaumHaSiddurHaShalemTheDailyPrayerBook1949/page/n496_medium.jpg"/><tei:head xml:lang="en">Psalm 128</tei:head><tei:p><tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/128/1"/>A Pilgrim Song. Happy is everyone who reveres the Lord, who walks in his ways. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/128/2"/>When you eat the toil of your hands, you shall be happy and at ease. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/128/3"/>Your wife shall be like a fruitful vine <tei:pb n="474" ed="1949 shabbat/minchah" facs="https://archive.org/download/PhilipBirnbaumHaSiddurHaShalemTheDailyPrayerBook1949/page/n498_medium.jpg"/>in the interior of your house; your children like olive plants, around your table. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/128/4"/>Behold, thus indeed shall the man be blessed who reveres the Lord. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/128/5"/>The Lord bless you from Zion; may you see the welfare of Jerusalem all the days of your life; <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/128/6"/>may you live to see your children’s children. Peace be upon Israel! <tei:milestone unit="verse"/></tei:p></tei:div>
